IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `raise-domain`
IMPORT `raise-definitions`
IMPORT `raise-reporting`
IMPORT `raise-penalty`
IMPORT `raise-seat`

-- New York Gen. Bus. Law Article 44-B (RAISE Act, as re-added by L. 2026, ch. 96) --
-- INDEPENDENT TESTS. A DRAFT. Not for use as advice.
--
-- Written by a session that did not see the encoding being built. Every expected value
-- was decided from the deposited bill texts (registers/source-bundle/, "ch96:N" is line N
-- of ny-s8828-2026-ch-96.txt) and written down in tests-independent-answers-first.md
-- BEFORE the encoding was opened; the encoding was then read only for its exported
-- questions, parameters and result types (raise-tests.l4 and NOTES.md were not read until
-- the assertions below had been run). No expectation was adjusted to match the code. A
-- failing assertion is a finding, left failing on purpose; each carries a comment naming
-- the provision and the reading behind it.
-- Weekdays and daylight-saving instants come from the system calendar (date -j,
-- TZ=America/New_York): 2027-03-14 and 2027-11-07 are the 2027 changes.
-- Readings taken (answers-first forks): F6-A the earlier trigger starts the 72-hour clock;
-- F7 exactly 72h00m is in time; F8-A hours are elapsed hours, so a daylight-saving change
-- does not stretch or shrink the window; F9-A the 24-hour disclosure does not replace the
-- 72-hour report; F11 § 1427 reaches a failed 24-hour disclosure; F13 a clock started
-- before 1 January 2027 is outside the re-added article.

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`indep YMD` y m d MEANS Date d m y

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, mo IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER, off IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `a moment`
`indep at` y mo d h mi off MEANS
    `a moment` WITH
        `the date`                     IS `indep YMD` y mo d
        `the hour`                     IS h
        `the minute`                   IS mi
        `the offset from UTC in hours` IS off

GIVETH A NUMBER
`indep EST` MEANS 0 - 5
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indep EDT` MEANS 0 - 4

§ `Independent fixtures`

-- Computing power, in operations (§ 1420(9)(a), ch96:148-150: "greater than 10^26").
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indep 10^25` MEANS 10000000000000000000000000
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indep 10^26` MEANS 100000000000000000000000000
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indep 10^26 + 1` MEANS 100000000000000000000000001
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indep 2 x 10^26` MEANS 200000000000000000000000000
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indep 3 x 10^26` MEANS 300000000000000000000000000

-- Is this a critical safety incident, for a foundation model I trained with 2 x 10^26
-- operations (a frontier model of mine); only the incident facts vary.
GIVEN w IS A BOOLEAN, wh IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A `what the model did`, mc IS A BOOLEAN
      single IS A BOOLEAN, people IS A NUMBER, dollars IS A NUMBER, public IS A BOOLEAN
      federal IS A BOOLEAN, loss IS A BOOLEAN, lossh IS A BOOLEAN, dec IS A BOOLEAN
      eval IS A BOOLEAN, risk IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`indep CSI` w wh c mc single people dollars public federal loss lossh dec eval risk MEANS
    `is this a critical safety incident` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 2 x 10^26`
        w wh c mc single people dollars public federal loss lossh dec eval risk

GIVETH A `what the model did`
`indep CBRN` MEANS `provided expert-level assistance in the creation or release of a chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapon`
GIVETH A `what the model did`
`indep no conduct` MEANS `none of the three kinds of conduct`

-- The 72-hour question for a kind (a) incident (weights exfiltrated, someone hurt) with a
-- frontier model of mine, in New York, no exception, no federal route; only the triggers vary.
GIVEN det IS A BOOLEAN, dd IS A DATE, dh IS A NUMBER, dm IS A NUMBER, doff IS A NUMBER
      rb IS A BOOLEAN, bd IS A DATE, bh IS A NUMBER, bm IS A NUMBER, boff IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `my duty to report to the office`
`indep 72h duty` det dd dh dm doff rb bd bh bm boff MEANS
    `must I report this incident to the office, and by when` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 2 x 10^26`
        TRUE TRUE `indep no conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        det dd dh dm doff rb bd bh bm boff TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- The same, reasonable belief only, with the coverage inputs and the model varying.
GIVEN trained IS A BOOLEAN, used IS A NUMBER, most IS A NUMBER, wh IS A BOOLEAN
      ny IS A BOOLEAN, college IS A BOOLEAN, empire IS A BOOLEAN, fed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `my duty to report to the office`
`indep 72h coverage` trained used most wh ny college empire fed MEANS
    `must I report this incident to the office, and by when` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE trained used most
        TRUE wh `indep no conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST`
        ny college empire fed

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, mo IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER, off IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `my duty to report to the office`
`indep report by` y mo d h mi off MEANS
    `report it to the office within 72 hours` (`indep at` y mo d h mi off)

-- The 24-hour question for the same kind (a) incident; imminent risk and coverage vary.
GIVEN most IS A NUMBER, wh IS A BOOLEAN, imminent IS A BOOLEAN
      ny IS A BOOLEAN, college IS A BOOLEAN, empire IS A BOOLEAN, fed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `my duty to disclose within 24 hours`
`indep 24h duty` most wh imminent ny college empire fed MEANS
    `must I disclose this incident within 24 hours` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE most most
        TRUE wh `indep no conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        imminent ny college empire fed

-- The § 1427 question for a foundation model I trained.
GIVEN most IS A NUMBER, revenues IS A NUMBER, f IS A `a failure of mine`, first IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `what I can be made to pay for the failure`
`indep AG` most revenues f first MEANS
    `what is the most the Attorney General can recover for this failure` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE most most revenues f first

GIVETH A `a failure of mine`
`indep 72h failure` MEANS `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the office within 72 hours`
GIVETH A `a failure of mine`
`indep 24h failure` MEANS `I failed to disclose an imminent-risk incident within 24 hours`

§ `(1) Am I a frontier developer? A large one? (§ 1420(6), (8)-(10), ch96:136-157)`

-- Exactly 10^26 does not meet "greater than 10^26".
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 10^26` `indep 10^26` EQUALS FALSE
-- One operation over the line.
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 10^26 + 1` `indep 10^26 + 1` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 2 x 10^26` EQUALS TRUE
-- Initiated a run that is at 10^25 so far but intended to reach 2 x 10^26 (§ 1420(8): "intends to use").
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 10^25` `indep 2 x 10^26` EQUALS TRUE
-- Not a foundation model (no broad data set): 2 x 10^26 operations on it does not make a frontier model.
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- Not an AI model at all.
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- I trained nothing (someone else's model, 2 x 10^26; no foundation model of my own).
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `indep 2 x 10^26` 0 EQUALS FALSE

-- Large: revenue with affiliates "in excess of five hundred million dollars" (ch96:155-157).
#ASSERT `am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 2 x 10^26` 500000000 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 2 x 10^26` 500000001 EQUALS TRUE
-- Not a frontier developer, whatever the revenue.
#ASSERT `am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 10^26` `indep 10^26` 1000000000000 EQUALS FALSE

§ `(2) Is this a critical safety incident? (§ 1420(3), (4), § 1423, ch96:96-129, 375-376)`

-- (a) weights exfiltrated, someone hurt.
#ASSERT `indep CSI` TRUE TRUE `indep no conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Weights exfiltrated, no death or bodily injury: not (a).
#ASSERT `indep CSI` TRUE FALSE `indep no conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Weights exfiltrated, $2bn property lost, no one hurt, none of (3)(a)(i)-(iii): neither (a) nor (b).
#ASSERT `indep CSI` TRUE FALSE `indep no conduct` TRUE TRUE 0 2000000000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (b) CBRN assistance, material contribution, single incident, 51 people.
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep CBRN` TRUE TRUE 51 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- (b) exactly 50 people: not "more than fifty" (reading F4-A).
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep CBRN` TRUE TRUE 50 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (b) property: $1,000,000,001 is; exactly $1,000,000,000 is not.
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep CBRN` TRUE TRUE 0 1000000001 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep CBRN` TRUE TRUE 0 1000000000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (b) not a single incident.
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep CBRN` TRUE FALSE 51 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (b) the model did not materially contribute.
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep CBRN` FALSE TRUE 51 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (b) excluded: publicly accessible information (ch96:110-112); lawful federal activity (ch96:113).
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep CBRN` TRUE TRUE 51 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep CBRN` TRUE TRUE 51 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (b) 100 people but none of the three kinds of conduct.
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep no conduct` TRUE TRUE 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (b) evading control, $2bn (ch96:107).
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `evaded the control of its frontier developer or user` TRUE TRUE 0 2000000000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- (c) loss of control with bodily injury; without it, not (c).
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep no conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep no conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (d) deception outside an eliciting evaluation, demonstrating materially increased risk.
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep no conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- (d) inside an evaluation designed to elicit it: not (d).
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep no conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- (d) no materially increased catastrophic risk: not (d).
#ASSERT `indep CSI` FALSE FALSE `indep no conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A model of exactly 10^26 operations is not a frontier model: weights exfiltrated with injury is not a CSI.
#ASSERT `is this a critical safety incident` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 10^26` `indep 10^26` TRUE TRUE `indep no conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Two kinds at once: (a) and (c).
#ASSERT `which kinds of critical safety incident is this` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 2 x 10^26` TRUE TRUE `indep no conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `kind (a), unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of model weights resulting in death or bodily injury`, `kind (c), loss of control of a frontier model causing death or bodily injury`

§ `(3) The 72-hour report to the office: who, and by when (§ 1422(3)(a), ch96:280-286)`

-- Friday evening: belief Fri 2027-01-08 18:00 EST -> Mon 2027-01-11 18:00 EST.
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` EQUALS `indep report by` 2027 1 11 18 0 `indep EST`
-- Determination only, same moment: the same deadline.
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` EQUALS `indep report by` 2027 1 11 18 0 `indep EST`
-- Across midnight: Thu 2027-01-07 23:30 -> Sun 2027-01-10 23:30 EST.
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 7) 23 30 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 7) 23 30 `indep EST` EQUALS `indep report by` 2027 1 10 23 30 `indep EST`
-- No weekend extension on the deposited text: Wed 2027-01-13 18:00 -> Sat 2027-01-16 18:00.
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 13) 18 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 13) 18 0 `indep EST` EQUALS `indep report by` 2027 1 16 18 0 `indep EST`
-- Spring-forward (2027-03-14): Fri 2027-03-12 20:00 EST -> 72 elapsed hours is Mon 2027-03-15
-- 21:00 EDT, which is 20:00 at the start's offset (-5). Wall-clock reading would give 20:00 EDT.
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 3 12) 20 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 3 12) 20 0 `indep EST` EQUALS `indep report by` 2027 3 15 20 0 `indep EST`
-- Fall-back (2027-11-07): Fri 2027-11-05 20:00 EDT -> Mon 2027-11-08 19:00 EST = 20:00 at -4.
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 11 5) 20 0 `indep EDT` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 11 5) 20 0 `indep EDT` EQUALS `indep report by` 2027 11 8 20 0 `indep EDT`
-- Both triggers, belief first (Mon 2027-02-01 09:00), determination later (Wed 2027-02-03 09:00):
-- F6-A, the earlier starts the clock -> Thu 2027-02-04 09:00.
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 2 3) 9 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 2 1) 9 0 `indep EST` EQUALS `indep report by` 2027 2 4 9 0 `indep EST`
-- Both triggers, determination first: still the earlier.
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 2 1) 9 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 2 3) 9 0 `indep EST` EQUALS `indep report by` 2027 2 4 9 0 `indep EST`
-- Leap day: Sat 2028-02-26 12:00 -> Tue 2028-02-29 12:00.
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2028 2 26) 12 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2028 2 26) 12 0 `indep EST` EQUALS `indep report by` 2028 2 29 12 0 `indep EST`
-- Year end: Thu 2027-12-30 12:00 -> Sun 2028-01-02 12:00.
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 12 30) 12 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 12 30) 12 0 `indep EST` EQUALS `indep report by` 2028 1 2 12 0 `indep EST`
-- Neither trigger yet: no clock.
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 2 1) 9 0 `indep EST` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 2 1) 9 0 `indep EST` EQUALS `no 72-hour clock yet, because I have neither determined that a critical safety incident occurred nor learned facts sufficient to establish a reasonable belief that one occurred`
-- Effective date (ch. 96 §§ 3, 5, ch96:470-488): belief Thu 2026-12-31 12:00 EST, before 1 Jan 2027 (F13).
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2026 12 31) 12 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2026 12 31) 12 0 `indep EST` EQUALS `not covered by this encoding, because my 72-hour clock started before the article takes effect on 1 January 2027`
-- Belief Fri 2027-01-01 12:00 EST, the first day: covered -> Mon 2027-01-04 12:00.
#ASSERT `indep 72h duty` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 1) 12 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 1) 12 0 `indep EST` EQUALS `indep report by` 2027 1 4 12 0 `indep EST`

-- Coverage (§§ 1425, 1426, 1422(9)) and who is bound.
-- Baseline: a frontier model of mine, someone hurt, New York, no exception -> report.
#ASSERT `indep 72h coverage` TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 2 x 10^26` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `indep report by` 2027 1 11 18 0 `indep EST`
#ASSERT `indep 72h coverage` TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 2 x 10^26` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered, because the model is not developed, deployed, or operating in whole or in part in New York state`
#ASSERT `indep 72h coverage` TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 2 x 10^26` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered, because I am excepted under section 1426 (accredited college or university doing academic research, or Empire AI)`
#ASSERT `indep 72h coverage` TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 2 x 10^26` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered, because I am excepted under section 1426 (accredited college or university doing academic research, or Empire AI)`
#ASSERT `indep 72h coverage` TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 2 x 10^26` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `deemed in compliance to the extent I meet the designated federal standard; send the office copies of the federal reports when I send them; failing that standard is a violation of the article`
-- Not a frontier developer (exactly 10^26).
#ASSERT `indep 72h coverage` TRUE `indep 10^26` `indep 10^26` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no duty, because I am not a frontier developer`
-- A frontier developer (another model at 3 x 10^26), but this frontier model is not one I trained.
#ASSERT `indep 72h coverage` FALSE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 3 x 10^26` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no duty, because the model is not one of my frontier models`
-- No one hurt: weights exfiltration alone is not a critical safety incident.
#ASSERT `indep 72h coverage` TRUE `indep 2 x 10^26` `indep 2 x 10^26` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no duty, because the incident is not a critical safety incident`

§ `(3) Did I report within 72 hours? Boundaries (§ 1422(3)(a))`

-- Belief Fri 2027-01-08 18:00 EST: 71h59m in time, 72h00m in time (F7), 72h01m late.
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 1 11) 17 59 `indep EST` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 1 11) 18 0 `indep EST` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 1 11) 18 1 `indep EST` EQUALS FALSE
-- Determination only, the same boundaries.
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 1 11) 18 0 `indep EST` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 1 11) 18 1 `indep EST` EQUALS FALSE
-- Across midnight: Thu 2027-01-07 23:30 -> Sun 2027-01-10 23:30 in time, 23:31 late.
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 7) 23 30 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 7) 23 30 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 1 10) 23 30 `indep EST` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 7) 23 30 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 7) 23 30 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 1 10) 23 31 `indep EST` EQUALS FALSE
-- Spring-forward: Fri 2027-03-12 20:00 EST; Mon 2027-03-15 21:00 EDT in time (72h00m elapsed),
-- 21:01 EDT late, 20:30 EDT in time (71h30m; the wall-clock reading F8-B would call it late).
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 3 12) 20 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 3 12) 20 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 3 15) 21 0 `indep EDT` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 3 12) 20 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 3 12) 20 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 3 15) 21 1 `indep EDT` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 3 12) 20 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 3 12) 20 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 3 15) 20 30 `indep EDT` EQUALS TRUE
-- Fall-back: Fri 2027-11-05 20:00 EDT; Mon 2027-11-08 19:00 EST in time, 19:01 EST late, 19:30 EST
-- late (72h30m; the wall-clock reading would call it in time).
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 11 5) 20 0 `indep EDT` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 11 5) 20 0 `indep EDT` (`indep YMD` 2027 11 8) 19 0 `indep EST` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 11 5) 20 0 `indep EDT` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 11 5) 20 0 `indep EDT` (`indep YMD` 2027 11 8) 19 1 `indep EST` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 11 5) 20 0 `indep EDT` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 11 5) 20 0 `indep EDT` (`indep YMD` 2027 11 8) 19 30 `indep EST` EQUALS FALSE
-- Reported in UTC: 2027-01-11 23:00 +0 is 18:00 EST (in time); 2027-01-12 00:00 +0 is 19:00 EST (late).
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 1 11) 23 0 0 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 1 8) 18 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 1 12) 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- Both triggers (F6-A): belief Mon 2027-02-01 09:00, determination Wed 2027-02-03 09:00.
-- Thu 2027-02-04 09:00 in time; Fri 2027-02-05 09:00 (48h after determination, 96h after belief) late.
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 2 3) 9 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 2 1) 9 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 2 4) 9 0 `indep EST` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 2 3) 9 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2027 2 1) 9 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 2 5) 9 0 `indep EST` EQUALS FALSE
-- Leap day: Sat 2028-02-26 12:00 -> Tue 2028-02-29 12:00 in time; Wed 2028-03-01 11:00 late.
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2028 2 26) 12 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2028 2 26) 12 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2028 2 29) 12 0 `indep EST` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (`indep YMD` 2028 2 26) 12 0 `indep EST` TRUE (`indep YMD` 2028 2 26) 12 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2028 3 1) 11 0 `indep EST` EQUALS FALSE

§ `(4) The 24-hour disclosure (§ 1422(3)(b), ch96:287-292)`

-- Imminent risk discovered: disclose within 24 hours AND still report to the office (F9-A).
#ASSERT `indep 24h duty` `indep 2 x 10^26` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `disclose it within 24 hours to an appropriate authority, such as a law enforcement or public safety agency with jurisdiction, and report it to the office within 72 hours as well`
#ASSERT `indep 24h duty` `indep 2 x 10^26` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no 24-hour duty, because I have not discovered that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury`
#ASSERT `indep 24h duty` `indep 10^26` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no 24-hour duty, because I am not a frontier developer`
#ASSERT `indep 24h duty` `indep 2 x 10^26` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no 24-hour duty, because the incident is not a critical safety incident`
#ASSERT `indep 24h duty` `indep 2 x 10^26` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered, because the model is not developed, deployed, or operating in whole or in part in New York state, for the 24-hour disclosure`
#ASSERT `indep 24h duty` `indep 2 x 10^26` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered, because I am excepted under section 1426, for the 24-hour disclosure`
-- § 1422(9)(b)(i): deemed compliance covers "subdivision three", (b) included.
#ASSERT `indep 24h duty` `indep 2 x 10^26` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `deemed in compliance with the 24-hour disclosure to the extent I meet the designated federal standard, and failing it is a violation of the article`

-- Boundaries: discovery Fri 2027-03-12 20:00 EST; Sat 2027-03-13 19:59 / 20:00 in time, 20:01 late.
#ASSERT `did I disclose within 24 hours` (`indep YMD` 2027 3 12) 20 0 `indep EST` (`indep YMD` 2027 3 13) 19 59 `indep EST` EQUALS TRUE
