§ `Report contents, amendments, FOIL, other regimes (§ 1422(1), (3)(c), (6), (8)-(10))`

#ASSERT `what must my report give` TRUE EQUALS LIST `item (a), the date of the critical safety incident`, `item (b), the reasons the incident qualifies as a critical safety incident`, `item (c), a short and plain statement describing the critical safety incident`, `item (d), whether the incident was associated with internal use of a frontier model`
-- The unused input changes nothing.
#ASSERT `what must my report give` FALSE EQUALS `what must my report give` TRUE
#ASSERT `may I file an amended report` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `may I file an amended report` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `may I file an amended report` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is my report exempt from FOIL` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is my report exempt from FOIL` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `does complying with another regime count` TRUE EQUALS `the designated federal standard counts, to the extent I meet it, while my declaration stands; I must copy my federal incident reports to the office when I send them, and failing that standard is a violation of the article`
-- No California or other-state clause: grep of ch96 for "california", "preempt", "other state": none.
#ASSERT `does complying with another regime count` FALSE EQUALS `nothing else counts: only a federal standard designated by the office, after a declaration to it, can stand in for section 1422(3), and the article gives no such effect to another state's law`

§ `(5) Penalties (§ 1427, ch96:393-405; § 1428(5), ch96:446-456)`

-- Large, failed 72-hour report: up to $1,000,000 first, $3,000,000 per subsequent.
#ASSERT `indep AG` `indep 2 x 10^26` 500000001 `indep 72h failure` TRUE EQUALS `a civil penalty that only the Attorney General may recover in a civil action` 1000000
#ASSERT `indep AG` `indep 2 x 10^26` 500000001 `indep 72h failure` FALSE EQUALS `a civil penalty that only the Attorney General may recover in a civil action` 3000000
-- Not large (exactly $500,000,000): no § 1427 penalty.
#ASSERT `indep AG` `indep 2 x 10^26` 500000000 `indep 72h failure` TRUE EQUALS `no civil penalty under section 1427, because I am not a large frontier developer`
-- Not a frontier developer at all, however rich.
#ASSERT `indep AG` `indep 10^26` 1000000000000 `indep 72h failure` TRUE EQUALS `no civil penalty under section 1427, because I am not a large frontier developer`
-- F11: "fails to report an incident as required by section [1422]" (ch96:400-401) read to include
-- the § 1422(3)(b) 24-hour disclosure.
-- THE NEXT TWO FAIL against the encoding, which answers "only if section 1427 reaches a failure
-- to disclose within 24 hours" (its F18). Left failing as the record of the disagreement; on the
-- source the text is open, leaning to the encoding ("disclose" in (3)(b), ch96:289, against
-- "report" in (3)(a) and "the initial report" in (3)(c), ch96:281, 294). See answers-first, step E.
#ASSERT `indep AG` `indep 2 x 10^26` 500000001 `indep 24h failure` TRUE EQUALS `a civil penalty that only the Attorney General may recover in a civil action` 1000000
#ASSERT `indep AG` `indep 2 x 10^26` 500000001 `indep 24h failure` FALSE EQUALS `a civil penalty that only the Attorney General may recover in a civil action` 3000000
#ASSERT `indep AG` `indep 2 x 10^26` 500000000 `indep 24h failure` TRUE EQUALS `no civil penalty under section 1427, because I am not a large frontier developer`

-- § 1428(5): $1,000 per day plus the assessments owed.
#ASSERT `what is the most the office may levy for a missing disclosure statement` 10 0 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `what is the most the office may levy for a missing disclosure statement` 0 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `what is the most the office may levy for a missing disclosure statement` 30 250000 EQUALS 280000
